{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-inbound-integration",
    "name": "Odoo Inbound Integration API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Inbound Integration API endpoints.\n\n**Endpoints (same for Demo Data and Real Data folders):**\n- `POST {{base_url}}/api/integration/order-details`\n- `POST {{base_url}}/api/integration/batch-closing`\n- `POST {{base_url}}/api/integration/fee-request`\n\n**Auth:** Set `auth_token` to the value configured in Odoo under Inbound Integration → Configuration → Settings. Sent as `Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}` (API-Key / X-API-Key also supported by the server).\n\n**Success response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"external_id\": \"229681\",\n  \"odoo_record_id\": 12345,\n  \"action\": \"created\"\n}\n```\n`action` is `created` (HTTP 201) or `updated` (HTTP 200).\n\n**Required fields:** `oid` (order-details), `batch_id` (batch-closing), `request_id` + `oids` (fee-request).\nProducts are matched by name / default_code on standard `product.product`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{auth_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8069",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "auth_token",
      "value": "YOUR_API_AUTH_TOKEN",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
